Subject: Freeze the Exynos CPU/GPU voltage policy thread during system sleep

The independent voltage-policy thread queries the fuel gauge directly, so
freezing the battery monitor workqueue does not stop this I2C path. Join
the system freezer before adapter interrupts are suspended. Resume the
existing low-voltage polling and frequency limits after thaw.

--- a/drivers/cpufreq/exynos-ufc.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/exynos-ufc.c
@@ -1194,7 +1194,10 @@
 	unsigned int lit_freq = 0;
 	unsigned int gpu_freq = 0;
 
-	while (!kthread_should_stop()) {
+	/* The fuel gauge uses interrupt-driven I2C, which stops in noirq. */
+	set_freezable();
+
+	while (!kthread_freezable_should_stop(NULL)) {
 		if (!cpu4_min_freq || !cpu0_min_freq) {
 			pr_warn_ratelimited("%s: VOL DVFS: waiting for cpufreq driver ...\n", __func__);
 			schedule_timeout_interruptible(msecs_to_jiffies(500));
@@ -1211,7 +1214,7 @@
 	sanitize_cpu_gpu_dvfs_vol();
 	pr_info("%s: VOL DVFS: kthread started successfully.\n", __func__);
 
-	while (!kthread_should_stop()) {
+	while (!kthread_freezable_should_stop(NULL)) {
 
 		vol = dvfs_get_dev_vol();
 
